    s.push_str("# a documentation team's spell checker, built on the docs themselves\nnew docs distance=2 case=0\nload_text_file data/corpus.txt\nstats\nfreq the\nfreq The\nfreq THE\nfreq don't\nfreq max_retries\nfreq 8080\nfreq kubernetes\ncontains Deploy\ncontains deployment\ncontains Operator's\nsplit Don't panic: it's 'quoted' -- a''b x_y 3.14 rock'n'roll users' end' _x_ 'tis\nsplit   leading and trailing   \nknown the The service deployment's 8080 2024 nan Infinity inf 1e5 1_000 x\nunknown the servise 8080 1__0 _1 1_ 1e 0x10 nan +nan -inf .5 5. ! ? ab\nknown ! . ' _ - a\nunknown ! . ' _ - a q\n# candidates and corrections\ncandidates service\ncorrection service\ncandidates Service\ncorrection Service\ncandidates servise\ncorrection servise\ncandidates srevice\ncorrection srevice\ncandidates servce\ncorrection servce\ncandidates sservice\ncorrection sservice\ncandidates dpeloyment\ncorrection dpeloyment\ncandidates deploymnt\ncorrection deploymnt\ncandidates polcy\ncorrection polcy\ncandidates plicy\ncorrection plicy\ncandidates 8080\ncorrection 8080\ncandidates 1e9\ncorrection 1e9\ncandidates nan\ncorrection nan\ncandidates token\ncorrection token\ncandidates tokne\ncorrection tokne\ncandidates toekn\ncorrection toekn\ncandidates tken\ncorrection tken\ncandidates tokens\ncorrection tokens\ncandidates zzzz\ncandidates q\ncorrection q\ncandidates qxz\ncandidates certificatesandmore\ncorrection certificatesandmore\ncandidates rools\ncorrection rools\ncandidates ro\ncorrection ro\ncandidates teh\ncorrection teh\ncandidates adn\ncorrection adn\ncandidates wiht\ned1 node\ned1 Node\ned1 8080\ned1 a\ned2 job\n# documents from the docs' review queue\ncheck A dedicated schedule caches every 10 hours. We'll keep the read-only registry for 90 hours befoe the routxe rolls.\ncheck Don't delete the custoa limit until the config waits. Every team writes its retry to a manual token on port 1.\ncheck Don't delete the weekly version until the window retries. Every registry wrrites its secret to a shared gateway on port 2024.\ncheck There isn't a automatic build for this zone; create one first. Mtost teams run one project per release and one server per service.\n");
    s.push_str("check It's safe to move a tepmorary operator to another response. After the certificate moves, the metric expires and the nightly worker is removed.\ncheck Use max_retries and log_level to ltune how the certificate publishes. If the config is private, the release starts and the dependency pauses.\ncheck Each secret has a active container and a nightly release. Yousr report can't reach the snapshot while the route is primary.\ncheck You can set the team route to 5 hours in the dashboard file. When a route reasd, the operator's backup shows a pending request.\ncheck Check that the gateway and the serivce use the same schedule version. If the owner is epmtcy, the client creates and the stage updates.\ncheck After the queue reloads, the rollout creates and the idle alert is removed. The 'dry run' mode shows what the team would do wthout changing the commit.\ncheck Use max_retries and log_level to tune how the deployment stops. A volume thalt rolls too ofwen is marked rublic and the quota reloads.\ncheck A build that writes too often is marked private and the table reports. Check that the lgimit and the network use the same table version.\ncheck The 'dry run' mode shows what the ubdget dould do without changing the branch. After the artifact blocks, the account rolls and the stale cluster is removed.\ncheck Use max_retries and log_level to tune how the report resumes. Your accoutn can't reach the server while the teaom is missing.\ncheck The file's cluster fails after 90 minutes. If the deployment is manual, the mirror cachegs and the route signs.\ncheck The sesion encrypts when the registry pauses. After the report updates, the job compresses and the active token is removed.\ncheck The nginx proxy reads the config files.\ncheck The service restarts when the config file updates.\ncheck \n# editing the dictionary\nadd Skiff 40\nadd skiff 2\nadd kubectl 5\nload_words Helm helm HELM nginx yaml\nstats\ncandidates skif\ncorrection skif\ncandidates kubctl\ncheck The skiff CLI wraps kubectl and helm; nginx reads yaml.\n");
    s.push_str("pop SKIFF\npop skiff\npop skiff\nfreq skiff\nremove nginx\nremove nginx\nremove_words yaml Helm nothing\nstats\nexport data/docs.json\nremove_threshold 3\nstats\ned1 node\ncandidates nod\ncorrection nod\nremove_threshold 1000000\nstats\ncandidates hello\ned1 hi\n# the exported dictionary, opened again\nopen saved data/docs.json\nstats\nfreq service\nfreq skiff\ncorrection servise\n# a checker that only looks one edit away\nnew strict distance=1 case=0\nload_text_file data/corpus.txt\ncandidates srevice\ncandidates srevcie\ncorrection srevcie\ndistance 2\ncandidates srevcie\ndistance 0\ndistance 3\ndistance 1\ncandidates tken\n# an empty checker\nnew empty distance=2 case=0\nstats\ncandidates hello\ncandidates hi\nknown hi\nunknown hi hello\ned1 ab\n# a case-sensitive checker for product names\nnew names distance=2 case=1\nload_text Skiff runs on Linux and macOS. The Skiff CLI talks to the Skiff API. skiff is the binary. The the THE.\nload_words Linux Linux linux API\nadd The 4\nstats\nknown Skiff skiff SKIFF Linux linux The the\nunknown Skiff skiff SKIFF Linux linux The the\ncandidates Skif\ncandidates skif\ncorrection Linx\ncorrection linx\ncandidates THe\ned1 Ab\nexport data/names.json\nopen folded data/names.json\nstats\nfreq the\nfreq skiff\nfreq linux\nfreq api\nuse saved\nstats\ncandidates srvice\n");
